{"ts":"2026-10-01T09:20:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Goal sheet evidence motion","status":"pending-review","axis":"motion","decision":"add row: new row drops in 6px (240ms power3.out) and takes focus; remove row: 140ms fade then re-draw with focus on Add row; Deloitte / Non-Deloitte switch: seg thumb slides, table crossfades in 10px from the side of travel (220ms); photo lands with a 0.96 to 1 scale (280ms)","reason":"each change is acknowledged where it happened, under 300ms, reduced motion skips all of it","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T11:05:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Page scrolling","status":"pending-review","axis":"motion","decision":"native scrolling everywhere: removed the Lenis smooth-scroll (lerp 0.12) and the unused ScrollTrigger plugin; programmatic scrolls use the browser's smooth scroll and respect reduced motion; drawer and search palette lock scroll with overflow hidden","reason":"user reported laggy scrolling; Lenis kept pages gliding ~700ms after the wheel stopped and tripled main-thread work while scrolling (800-1070ms vs 180ms measured on the goal sheet); Doherty threshold and Jakob's law favour the platform's own scroll","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T11:05:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Page background","status":"pending-review","axis":"structure","decision":"page gradient moved from background-attachment: fixed on body to a fixed body::before layer; the top bar paints the same gradient sized to the window and offset by its own left edge (--tb-x, --vw, --vh set in app.js on shell render, resize and font load)","reason":"a fixed background attachment repaints the window on every scroll frame; pixel diff against the old rendering is zero in light and dark, desktop and phone, top and scrolled","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T11:05:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Goal sheet Previous months","status":"pending-review","axis":"structure","decision":"the employee's Previous months card leads the Monthly review, above the review header; the month on screen is always in its list (a month opened from further back takes the third slot) and the separate Back link is dropped in favour of the card's own","reason":"user asked for it at the top of the page","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
