{"ts":"2026-10-01T13:10:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Quarterly evidence","status":"pending-review","axis":"structure","decision":"Quarterly keeps the goal sheet table and adds the review-deck evidence cards below it under an icon-led heading (Review deck evidence · category · Weightage N%); a quarter's evidence is seeded from its months' rows; open reviews get a per-form Bring in N rows from Apr-Jun (with Undo); goal 11 rolls up the three months' status reviews; table rows and cards link to each other","reason":"user asked for the PPT content in Quarterly alongside the Excel table, with weightage; rolling up the months avoids typing the evidence twice","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T13:10:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Weightage wording","status":"pending-review","axis":"typography","decision":"one word and unit everywhere: 'Weightage N%' on goal cards, table group cells and total rows (was 'Weight N%' on cards and a bare number in the table); supersedes the Weight % detail in the 1 Oct monthly form entry","reason":"critique P2: two words and two units for the same figure; the review deck writes 'Weightage: N%'","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T13:10:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Goal sheet section motion and focus","status":"pending-review","axis":"motion","decision":"segment switches enter from the side of travel (120ms fade, 300ms power3.out, 40ms stagger); a review link or month clicked inside the panel moves focus to the new panel; table/card jumps glide with native smooth scroll and the 1.4s highlight starts on scrollend (700ms fallback); brought-in rows drop in 6px with a 40ms stagger, then flash","reason":"interaction-design pass: focus was lost when the clicked control was replaced, and the jump highlight was half-faded on arrival","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T14:20:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Risks and dependencies form","status":"pending-review","axis":"structure","decision":"a third option, Internal, beside Deloitte and Non-Deloitte, with the Non-Deloitte columns (team rather than client dependencies in its flow and focus line); internal staff open on it; the switch slides and the table enters from the side of travel across three options","reason":"user asked for an Internal button with the same table as Non-Deloitte","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T14:20:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Financial year","status":"pending-review","axis":"structure","decision":"quarters are labelled by FY (Apr-Mar) app-wide, e.g. 'Q1 FY 2026–27 (Apr–Jun 2026)'; monthly reviews show their FY quarter; yearly goals are scored in FY Q4 (Jan–Mar), whose total is out of 100; Annual, the quarterly tracker and the status-review strip cover the FY; quarter keys stay calendar-named IDs","reason":"user: our year is April to March","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T16:40:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Review metadata across the platform","status":"pending-review","axis":"content","decision":"form names and version labels (v1/v2/v3, 'Goal sheet BA & Sr BA v1') removed from every screen; the Form column dropped from all review tables; history, locked and override notes now say 'goals and reviewer'; Admin config lists forms by name only","reason":"user asked to remove versions and the Form column everywhere; the review type and period carry the meaning users need","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T16:40:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Review tables · Review type column","status":"pending-review","axis":"typography","decision":"'Cycle' column renamed 'Review type'; cell leads with the type (Monthly/Quarterly, 520 weight, ink-2) and the period muted after it, so the employee name stays the row's one bold anchor","reason":"user rename; critique flagged three bold anchors per row","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T16:40:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Review Completion · Awaiting manager","status":"pending-review","axis":"structure","decision":"quarterly-only everywhere on the page: the filter pill (tooltip states the scope), the KPI ('Awaiting manager', sub 'Quarterly reviews only') and By reviewer 'Awaiting them' (header tooltip), so the per-reviewer column sums to the pill count","reason":"user asked for Awaiting manager to be quarterly only; critique P1 found the reviewer column still counting monthly","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T16:40:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Review table filter swap","status":"pending-review","axis":"motion","decision":"old rows fade 90ms ease-out, the table height glides (power2.inOut, max 300ms) instead of jumping, only rows in view rise 6px with the whole stagger held under 200ms; review tables use fixed column shares so columns never slide between filters; a second click mid-swap wins; reduced motion swaps instantly; an aria-live line announces the filter and count","reason":"interaction-design pass: Doherty threshold (rows begin ~170ms after click), no layout jump, stagger budget for 60-row lists","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
{"ts":"2026-10-01T18:30:00Z","project":"NV-DPS-Internal","surface":"Revenue, Cost & Profit block (Practice Overview, Financial Performance, Team Financials)","status":"pending-review","axis":"structure","decision":"supersedes the 30 Sep Revenue & Budget hero: the block leads with the year's Revenue (hero), Cost and Profit; the practice has no Budget tile, marker, chart tick, table column or trend goal line (metrics grid drops to three columns, the hero takes its own row at <=1180px); a team keeps a fourth Budget tile and its markers; the outlook becomes 'How the year adds up', a ledger of actual + forecast = revenue, CTC + ₹3 L × people = cost, profit and margin; the month table gains a Revenue column (what each month counts as) and a year total row","reason":"user's formulas: revenue = actuals where available plus forecasts, cost = (CTC + ₹3 lakh) per person, profit = revenue − cost, and no budget or financial target at practice level; the ledger lets anyone check each figure against the one above it","source":"agent-pending","promote":false}
